-- 1163: Blog post - "Can You Grow Melons Hydroponically in Singapore? Our 11 October 2025 Class Says Yes"
--
--       Companion post to 1162 - hydroponics beyond leafy greens (rockmelon), written
--       around the 11 October 2025 class.
--       Ships already published (status 1); linkedin_urn carries the manual-skip
--       sentinel so publishDue / the share cron never pick it up.
--       published_at is pinned to 2025-10-11 (the class date), NOT CURDATE().
--
-- Every course figure below was read off the LIVE course page on 2026-08-29:
--   * Fee card: full $350.00, GST $31.50 (9%), baseline nett $206.50 (SG/PR 21+, 50%),
--     MCES/SME nett $136.50 (SG 40+, 70%).
--   * Course information: 1 day / 8 hrs, Beginner, 1 hr assessment.
--   * Venue: MEOD Farm, 13 Neo Tiew Harvest Lane, Singapore 719838.
--   * Funding validity 24 Mar 2025 - 23 Mar 2027.
--   * Skills Framework TSC: Urban Farming Implementation and Management Control
--     (AGR-FOP-2002-1.1). LO1-LO2 quoted from the course page.
--
-- Class photographs supplied by the academy, cropped to landscape and uploaded to R2
-- under blog/hydroponics/ (all verified HTTP 200). Embedded as <figure
-- class="mmd-blog-figure"> with credit in the figcaption, per
-- feedback_blog_press_photo_crop_from_supplied_scan.
--
-- External sources cited in the body (all verified HTTP 200 on 2026-08-29):
--   * SFA "Hydroponics: Getting to the Root of the Myths" (30-by-30, nutrient myths,
--     Scientia Horticulturae vitamin-C comparison, sub-$100 beginner kit).
--   * SFA farm profiles for ComCrop and Sustenir Agriculture.
--   * Business Times on Greenphyto's 23m vertical farm (45x output figure attributed
--     to the article, not stated as our own research).
--   * NUS Enterprise startup story for Singrow.
--
-- Notes for future editors:
--  * apply.php splits statements on ";" at end-of-line - the content HTML is ONE line.
--  * Content is pure ASCII (em-dashes etc. as HTML entities) - see
--    feedback_migration_applyphp_utf8_outage; a raw UTF-8 byte here can 502 every host.
--  * The excerpt DOES use real UTF-8 em-dashes (written via CHAR(...) so this file stays
--    ASCII) because it is reused as PLAIN TEXT by the LinkedIn/newsletter copy - see 1161.
--  * FAQ ships as native <details> accordions per the blog-pipeline rules.
--  * Idempotent: WHERE NOT EXISTS on url_key, INSERT IGNORE on tag links. Safe to re-run.
